From cde9c98fbb1ef98d2672eb8ebfe722e0660bcfc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:25:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: Raise the tuna skin thresholds for quiet_therm
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sys-therm-3 thresholds (48/49/50°C) assume a sensor that tracks the
skin. quiet_therm is a board thermistor that runs hotter: on onyx it
crosses 49°C a few minutes into a game with the battery at 35-38°C, so the
framework reports MODERATE and games cut their frame rate and quality
while the device is only warm. Raise LIGHT/MODERATE/SEVERE to
52/54/56°C. CRITICAL and above are unchanged, and mi_thermald and
thermal-engine still do the actual throttling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kye574qt5dotSwvkUkvhEe
---
 thermalConfig.cpp | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/thermalConfig.cpp b/thermalConfig.cpp
index 63abbff..4fb7f35 100644
--- a/thermalConfig.cpp
+++ b/thermalConfig.cpp
@@ -2490,9 +2490,9 @@ namespace thermal {
 			{ "quiet_therm" },
 			"skin",
 			{
-			[LIGHT] = 48000,
-			[MODERATE] = 49000,
-			[SEVERE] = 50000,
+			[LIGHT] = 52000,
+			[MODERATE] = 54000,
+			[SEVERE] = 56000,
 			[CRITICAL] = 60000,
 			[EMERGENCY] = 61000,
 			[SHUTDOWN] = 90000,
-- 
